  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nClouds will continue to stream northward across the area from the\nremnants of Hurricane Isaias. Winds will pick up during the day with\ngusty winds by this afternoon. Wind gusts of 25 to 35 mph will be \npossible. Gusty winds will start to decrease during the second half \nof the night tonight. One half to one and a half inches of rain is \nforecast across a large portion of the area, however locally higher \namounts of two inches will be possible. The system will start to move\nout of the area Sunday evening.\n\nKey Message 2)\nDry conditions are expected for Monday. Otherwise, multiple systems\nwill work through the region during the week. There are some timing\nand strength differences with the models. There is not a lot of\ninstability therefore thunder, while possible, will be limited.",
